<!doctype HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd">
<!--#include file="helpVar.asp"-->
<HTML>
<HEAD>
   <TITLE>Help Advanced </TITLE>
   <META content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type">
   <LINK href="helpStyle.css" rel="stylesheet" title="WebEnabled" type="text/css">
</HEAD>
<BODY>
   <TABLE border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
      <!-- Begin logos row - middle logo is instrument specific -->
      <TR bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
         <TD bgcolor="#FFFFFF" height="60" valign="MIDDLE" width="230">
            <IMG alt="Agilent" border="0" height="60" src="../image/agilent.gif" width="230">
         </TD>
         <TD bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" height="60" valign="top">
            <IMG alt="" src="../image/instrumentBanner.gif"></TD>
      </TR>
      <!-- End logos row -->
      <TR>
         <TD bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" colspan="2">
            <IMG alt="" height="2" src="../image/filltrans.gif"></TD>
      </TR>
   </TABLE>
   <H1>
      Welcome Page Help</H1>
   <P>
      The <I>Agilent Technologies</I> web pages for the
      <%=sModel%>&nbsp; will assist you in getting your system up and running as quickly
      as possible. If you have trouble with the instrument, you may contact Agilent by
      clicking on the "Support" link that appears on the top banner of the web pages.
      On the left side of the
      <%=sModel%>&nbsp;web pages, you will find a column of Navigation tabs. Use these
      tabs to select which part of the instrument to view or modify. See the <A href="helpNav.asp?Model=<%Response.Write sModel%>">
         Navigation Help Page</A>&nbsp;for more explanation on each of these Navigation
      tabs.
   </P>
   <P>
      The <B>Welcome Page </B>displays the basic information about the Agilent
      <%=sModel%>. This information can be used in forming the addresses needed to run
      SICL or VISA programs. The information cannot be modified on the Welcome Page. You
      must use the "Configure Network" page for that.
   </P>
   <P>
      The display includes:
   </P>
   <UL>
      <LI>Instrument
         <P>
            This field shows the instrument model number and name.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Serial Number
         <P>
            This field shows the serial number for this instrument.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Description
         <P>
            This field shows the description of the instrument that is used throughout its web
            pages.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Hostname
         <P>
            This value shows the Internet domain name for the instrument. If this field is blank,
            then the instrument could not determine its name. This could be because the instrument
            doesn't have access to a DNS server. Depending upon what type of servers that you
            have, you may be able to use this name to connect to the instrument.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>IP Address
         <P>
            This field shows the IP address of the instrument. The currently displayed IP Address
            may have been established by one of three ways:</P>
         <UL>
            <LI>The address was served by a DHCP server during boot. </LI>
            <LI>DHCP is turned off or unavailable on the network and the IP address was selected
               using Automatic Private IP Addressing (AutoIP). </LI>
            <LI>DHCP is turned off or unavailable on the network, AutoIP is turned off and the
               static IP address was used. </LI>
         </UL>
         <P>
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>VISA TCP/IP Connect String
         <P>
            This field shows a connect string that may be used when making a programmatic connection
            with VISA over TCP/IP.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Advanced Information
         <P>
            Click on this button to hide the advanced information
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Identification
         <P>
            The Identification control enables a front panel indication of the instrument serving
            the web page. This is very helpful when you need to physically locate a specific
            instrument within a group of instruments.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Firmware Revision
         <P>
            This field shows the revision number for the firmware. You may need this if you
            have to call support for this instrument.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Ethernet (MAC) Address
         <P>
            This is the Media Access Control Address, also known as the link-level address,
            the Ethernet (station) Address, the LANIC ID and Hardware Address. This is a unique
            48-bit address assigned by the manufacturer for each Internet device. It is usually
            seen as 12 hexadecimal characters, sometimes with colon or dash separators between
            every two characters (e.g. "00:03:d3:00:00:17" or "00-03-d3-00-00-17 ").
         </P>
         <P>
            Your IT department may need this number if they are assigning a static IP address
            for this device.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>SCPI TCP/IP Socket Port
         <P>
            This field shows the port number used by the TCP/IP socket interface.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>SCPI Telnet Port
         <P>
            This field shows the port number used by the SCPI telnet interface.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>VISA USB Connect String
         <P>
            This field shows a connect string that may be used when making a programmatic connection
            with VISA over USB.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>SICL Interface Name
         <P>
            This field shows the Remote SICL Interface Name that must be used when configuring
            the
            <%=sModel%>
            as a GPIB VISA LAN Client in Agilent's IO Libraries Configuration, IO Config.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>GPIB Address
         <P>
            This is the current GPIB address of the instrument.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>LXI Class
         <P>
            This instrument is certified to LXI Class C conformance.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>LXI Version
         <P>
            This is the version of the LXI standard to which the instrument was tested.
         </P>
      </LI>
      <LI>Auto-MDIX
         <P>
            Whether the instrument provides <I>medium dependent interface crossover</I>. This
            capability allows direct connection to the instrument without using a crossover
            cable.
         </P>
      </LI>
   </UL>
</BODY>
</HTML>
